  "body": {
    "id": "prop:sharp-margin-modulus",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For every \\(\\alpha>0\\), \\(h<c\\), and sufficiently small \\(0<\\rho<\\min\\{h,1-c\\}\\), the construction \\((P_{\\mathrm{lf}},\\eta_{\\mathrm{lf}})\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm m}(\\alpha,h^{-\\alpha})\\), satisfies \\(\\|s-e\\|_\\infty=\\rho\\) with the true outcome regressions, and obeys \\[R(P_{\\mathrm{lf}},\\eta_{\\mathrm{lf}})=\\frac{\\delta\\alpha}{(\\alpha+1)h^\\alpha}\\rho^{1+\\alpha}.\\] Hence the exponent \\(1+\\alpha\\) cannot be improved uniformly for this unsmoothed one-step correction over the stated cap-shell class. This is sharpness of the correction modulus, not a minimax lower bound over all estimators.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "alpha",
      "rho",
      "h",
      "c",
      "P_lf",
      "eta_lf",
      "mathcal_M_margin",
      "s",
      "e",
      "R_eta",
      "delta"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:punctured-margin",
