      "lem:exact-branch-remainder"
    ],
    "justification": "The equality witness distinguishes a sharp cap-crossing modulus from a merely sufficient margin bound.",
    "gap": "Audibert and Tsybakov establish the generic classification exponent; the legal causal witness preserves the capped intervention, treatment law, bounded outcomes, and exact one-step signal.",
    "consumer": "Method developers obtain a hard threshold for nuisance rates below which the unsmoothed correction cannot have negligible root-\\(n\\) bias.",
    "proof_tex": "Under the construction, \\(e=c-U\\in(c-h,c]\\subset(0,1)\\), so the Bernoulli treatment law is legal; \\(Y=A\\in[0,1]\\subset[-M,M]\\), and hence the bounded-outcome condition holds.  Since \\(P(U=0)=0\\), there is no propensity atom at \\(c\\).  For every admissible \\(t\\),\n\\begin{equation}\n P_{\\mathrm{lf}}\\{0<|e(X)-c|\\le t\\}\n =P(0<U\\le t)\n =\\begin{cases}(t/h)^\\alpha,&t\\le h,\\\\1,&t>h,\n \\end{cases}\n \\le h^{-\\alpha}t^\\alpha.                                                               \\tag{19}\n\\end{equation}\nThus \\(P_{\\mathrm{lf}}\\in\\mathcal M_{\\mathrm m}(\\alpha,h^{-\\alpha})\\).  The candidate satisfies \\(s-e=\\rho\\) everywhere, so\n\\(\\|s-e\\|_\\infty=\\rho\\), and it uses \\(u_a=\\mu_a\\), making the propensity--outcome product in the exact remainder zero.\n\nThe true propensity is below the cap almost surely.  The candidate is on the saturated branch exactly when \\(U\\le\\rho\\), up to the null endpoint convention.  Since \\(\\tau=1\\), the exact remainder identity therefore reduces to\n\\begin{equation}\n R(P_{\\mathrm{lf}},\\eta_{\\mathrm{lf}})\n =\\delta E[U\\mathbf1\\{U\\le\\rho\\}].                                                     \\tag{20}\n\\end{equation}\nThe distribution of \\(U\\) has density \\(\\alpha u^{\\alpha-1}/h^\\alpha\\) on \\((0,h)\\).  Because \\(\\rho<h\\), direct integration gives\n\\begin{equation}\n E[U\\mathbf1\\{U\\le\\rho\\}]\n =\\frac{\\alpha}{h^\\alpha}\\int_0^\\rho u^\\alpha\\,du\n =\\frac{\\alpha}{(\\alpha+1)h^\\alpha}\\rho^{1+\\alpha}.                                   \\tag{21}\n\\end{equation}\nEquations (20)--(21) prove the equality.  Any uniform upper modulus of smaller order than \\(\\rho^{1+\\alpha}\\) for this same unsmoothed correction and nuisance neighborhood would contradict this member of the class, establishing the stated, procedure-specific sharpness.",
